<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Redefinition of MAUI's Maui.SplashTheme. One item differs from the library's version;
  everything else is reproduced verbatim, including the parent chain.

  WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST
  =========================
  .NET MAUI 10.0.101 has no way to change how the Android 12+ splash icon is sized. Its
  library Maui.SplashTheme (Microsoft.Maui.Controls, res/values/styles.xml) reads:

    <style name="Maui.SplashTheme" parent="Maui.MainTheme.NoActionBar">
        <item name="maui_splash">true</item>
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@drawable/maui_splash</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/maui_splash_color</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/maui_splash</item>
    </style>

  and the library's own res/drawable/maui_splash.xml is a LAYER-LIST with
  android:opacity="opaque" whose first item is a solid @color/maui_splash_color fill. So
  windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon points at the whole layer-list, background fill included,
  and the system treats all of it as icon content and masks it into the icon shape. That is
  the reported "tiny logo on an oddly shaped navy patch": the fill becomes a navy disc and
  the logo is whatever is left of it inside the mask.

  Compounding it, the Resizetizer-generated drawable-v31/maui_splash_image.xml hard-codes
  the bitmap into a 108dp box:

    <item android:width="108dp" android:height="108dp" android:gravity="center">

  Android's spec for that area is 240x240dp (160dp visible circle) with an icon background,
  or 288x288dp (192dp visible circle) without. 108dp of 240dp is 45% of the intended size.
  MAUI 10.0.101 exposes no attribute, metadata or property to change that box, has no
  windowSplashScreenIconBackgroundColor, no postSplashScreenTheme, no day/night variant,
  and generates no values-v31 at all. A project-level resource is the documented extension
  point, so the theme is redefined here.

  THE PARENT CHAIN, WHICH IS THE PART THAT IS EASY TO BREAK
  ========================================================
  Redeclaring a style does not merge it with the library's, so every item the app's chrome
  depends on has to come from somewhere. The chain is reproduced exactly:

    Maui.SplashTheme
      -> Maui.MainTheme.NoActionBar      (windowActionBar=false, windowNoTitle=true,
                                          windowActionModeOverlay=true, actionMode*)
        -> Maui.MainTheme                (empty in MAUI 10; the v35+ edge-to-edge hook)
          -> Maui.MainTheme.Base         (Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight, colorPrimary,
            |                             colorPrimaryDark, colorAccent, appBarLayoutStyle,
            |                             bottomNavigationViewStyle, materialButtonStyle,
            |                             checkboxStyle, alertDialogTheme,
            |                             materialAlertDialogTheme, maui_edgetoedge_optout)
            -> Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight

  These are the library's own styles, referenced by name, not copies - only Maui.SplashTheme
  itself is replaced. Nothing in the app's chrome is redefined, so the app's windows, dialogs,
  buttons and checkboxes keep the exact attributes they had.

  The only change is windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon, which now points at an icon-only vector
  with no background fill and an intrinsic size of 288dp instead of a 108dp layer-list box.
  See drawable/cafepos_splash_icon.xml for the arithmetic and the expected result.

  WHY THIS IS IN values/ AND NOT values-v31/
  ===========================================
  Because that is where MAUI puts these attributes itself - the shipped Maui.SplashTheme above
  is in res/values/, not res/values-v31/ - and it builds. AAPT2 compiles against
  targetSdkVersion=36, so windowSplashScreenBackground and windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon
  resolve; on API 21-30 the platform simply ignores the two attributes it does not know, and
  the pre-31 path is carried entirely by android:windowBackground, which is unchanged.

  API 21-30, unchanged from before: @drawable/maui_splash is a layer-list of the navy
  @color/maui_splash_color with the splash bitmap centred over it. The bitmap is now the
  redesigned mark on a transparent background (the old artwork had a navy disc on a navy
  background, so only the gold cup ever read), 89dp across on the 128dp BaseSize raster.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Maui.SplashTheme" parent="Maui.MainTheme.NoActionBar">
        <item name="maui_splash">true</item>
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@drawable/maui_splash</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/maui_splash_color</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/cafepos_splash_icon</item>
    </style>
</resources>
